[Music]  all right thank you I'm thanks Tim  Burley for the invitation in fact when  she originally invited me to submit a  proposal I was thinking well I I don't  know what I do in canvas that is special  or is different from what other people  do I've never seen the competition I've  certainly never used quizzes or or some  of these embedding of multimedia  material on canvas essentially sort of  sums up the way that I've been using  canvas and I think it boils down to the  way that I've used the homepage as the  go-to resource for a lot of things that  we do in class so just to give you a bit  of background knowing right here is a  pretty large statistics class there's  about a hundred students and we don't  have regular quizzes and tests we do  have sort of two exams throughout the  semester but we do have regular reading  assignments and homework assignments and  so on so one of the questions that I'm  sure you all have from students is sort  of what's what's the homework or what's  the reading assignment where can I find  this that we did in class and for me the  easiest way to just put everything in a  central place has been to make use of  the homepage this is just one of the  pages that I've created and I sort of  clicked to set it as the homepage and I  designed it to be sort of a growing  syllabus if you will so initially it'll  be a week 1 of class and you probably  won't see very much beyond say up to  this point and so there will be  essential information like who are the  TAS in the course who are the you LA's  we use you always in this course as well  when are there office hours and all this  is dynamic in the sense that we can  change it at any time it's so it's a  website that we can sort of go in modify  as needed in order to get sort of the  most up-to-date information so and the  way that things progressed is obviously  you know the important things are way at  the top and then I like to organize my  material on a week to week basis so I  try to have a top level heading per week  it's just week one the date what did we  cover in class what are the slides that  go along  with a material in class and what are  some sort of computer code examples that  would come along with that I mean I  think that this gives me just a very  nice way of pointing students to the  page I can even say things like if you  happen to miss class feel free to just  keep up to date by looking at what's  going on on the homepage everything is  posted there you wouldn't miss anything  the only that's missing is maybe videos  of our in-class lectures but I'm very  resistant against that kind of thing  things that that I would want to  highlight is I did try doing something  like this with the modules section of  canvas and I heard a lot of you use  canvas very successfully so I do have a  slight example from an earlier a  different course when I did try to  implement the same kind of thing using  modules and I thought this would make my  life easier because I could just go  ahead and create these high-level  folders from week to week I can include  assignments I can include any other  files that I'd like to include normally  and by what I found is that this is a  little less flexible it's much harder  for me to format the names of things  include bold facing for things I'd like  to highlight I'm and it takes up a lot  of space so week 1 for this class for  example stretches what fold page  basically I just scroll down to get to  week 2 and whereas I tend now to prefer  just having everything on this home page  where I can even have things that are  just just text right so things like when  office hours are links to practice exams  solutions to practice exams having it  all be in that one central place seems  to me the easiest way to go I guess they  still have time remaining so since this  is not a canvas propaganda session I  think I want to also talk a little bit  about the struggles that I've had with  canvas if I may since I have an audience  and so in my class we have about four  people five people grading for every  single assignment and we do make use of  canvases grading tool I really do like  the speed grader that everybody can go  in and see the PDF submissions they can  annotate the PDFs work with a rubric  and this makes it really easy if you  don't want people to be swapping back  and forth paper assignments for example  one challenge that I've had however is  that if you have multiple people grading  simultaneously the rubric be very  careful because they will sometimes  overwrite each other's points and I've  had that when two graders were grading  simultaneously someone may be grading  problem one someone grading problem five  and maybe they're just offset by a  couple of students and somebody will  click on submit and save and boom the  other grade completely disappears into  thin air so I'm hoping that someday  we're able to resolve this I see this as  sort of the main complaint that I have  with canvas in the meantime but  otherwise I think the students have been  fairly satisfied with being able to have  everything in in one place oops sorry  about that and and being able to sort of  see their grades see their feedback and  being able to submit things very easily  without having to appear in person to  turn things in that's all I'm I don't  know if I understood you clearly so  presume to teach and fellows are grading  simultaneously the same assignment they  would be doing it why is it accidental  or you deliberately assigned like the TF  one will grade problems one to two and  tf2 will great problems three to four I  mean why would that problem occur that's  a very good question so in in my mind  because we want to have our you all A's  and TAS grade consistently we want to  instead of having them great different  students maybe they just create  different problems and that way  everybody you know one TF will greet all  of problem one one table grade all the  problem two and so in that case it is  possible for two of them to be grading  the same person simultaneously  can you set it so that the students  receive an email announcement when you  update the homepage I have not figured  out how to do that that would certainly  be ideal I should look into that I think  that would be an excellent sort of  improvement upon the current system to  have students see that new material has  been posted I don't think that happens  on pages unfortunately it is assignments  you can do it for assignments but not on  pages right now okay someday thank you  very much  [Applause]  [Music]

